From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: a tap is a tap, an empty tray holds nothing, a mark waits for its place

Three things the owner met on a touchscreen laptop in one evening.

A tap on the clock or on Quick Options opened arrange mode instead of the
menu, every time, while a tap on a dock tile was fine. The shelf ran its
own timer from the press and cancelled it when it saw the release -- and a
button takes the touch sequence for itself, so that release never reached
the shelf at all: the timer ran on under a finger that had already lifted.
Clutter's own press gesture sees both ends of a press wherever it goes and
arbitrates with the button's click gesture, so a quick release is the
button's and a held finger is an arrangement. The gesture goes on the
islands and on the parts inside them -- the clock, Quick Options, the tray
-- because that is where the touch goes.

A tray with nothing in it held width. An extension indicator can be visible
and draw nothing, and what the person is left looking at is a hole in the
bar where their tray used to be. The tray is now there while it has
something to show, like the notification island, and the space it would
have taken goes back to the band.

And a running-window mark that had never been placed was faded anyway,
which asks Clutter to update the stage views of an actor that does not know
where it is. It said so, many times a minute, in the person's journal. A
mark fades when it is placed.

Known limit, said plainly: with the gesture in place a tap is a tap
everywhere, but a long press on the clock or Quick Options does not yet
open arrange mode in the harness -- their own buttons take the sequence in
a way the gesture beside them does not see. A long press on any other
island, on a dock icon, or a right-click, still gets there, and the island
menu still carries Arrange Islands.

---
diff --git a/js/ui/lumaDockWindows.js b/js/ui/lumaDockWindows.js
index 4b4dc79..8682a41 100644
--- a/js/ui/lumaDockWindows.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaDockWindows.js
@@ -94,13 +94,22 @@ class WindowMark extends St.Widget {
             this.remove_style_class_name(this.kind);
         this.kind = kind;
         this.add_style_class_name(kind);
-        this._fade();
+        // A mark that has never been placed has no allocation yet: easing it
+        // asks Clutter to update the stage views of an actor that does not
+        // know where it is, which it says so about, many times a minute, in
+        // the person's journal. It fades when it is placed.
+        if (this.box)
+            this._fade();
     }
 
     // Ink at 55% for every mark except the focused pill, which is full ink.
     _fade(target = this.kind === 'focused' ? 255 : 140) {
         this.remove_transition('opacity');
-        this.ease({opacity: target, duration: animations() && this.box ? MARK_TIME : 0,
+        if (!this.box) {
+            this.opacity = target;
+            return;
+        }
+        this.ease({opacity: target, duration: animations() ? MARK_TIME : 0,
             mode: Clutter.AnimationMode.EASE_OUT_QUAD});
     }
 
